---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../../../components/PageIntro.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="0003. License .github community infrastructure under CC BY-SA 4.0 | Macro Evidence"
  description="Governance decision 0003: License .github community infrastructure under CC BY-SA 4.0. Status: Superseded."
>
  <PageIntro
    kicker="Governance decision"
    title="0003. License .github community infrastructure under CC BY-SA 4.0"
    lead="Governance decision 0003 of the Macro Evidence Governance decision series."
  />

  <section class="section policy-page">
    <div class="site-container reading policy-reading-wide">
      <article class="policy-text">
        <p class="policy-status">
          <strong>Status:</strong>&#32;Superseded<br />&#32;<strong
            >Superseded by:</strong
          >&#32;<a
            href="/governance/decisions/0011-use-mixed-licensing-for-github-community-content-and-executable-automation"
            >decision 0011</a
          >
        </p>
        <h2 id="context">Context</h2>
        <p>
          The&#32;<code>macro-evidence/.github</code>&#32;repository provides
          Macro Evidence's public organization profile and organization-wide
          default community health infrastructure, including contribution
          guidance, security reporting guidance, pull request and issue
          templates, and contributor conduct policy.
        </p>
        <p>
          The repository has been published under Creative Commons Attribution
          4.0 International (CC BY 4.0). That license permits reuse, adaptation,
          redistribution, and commercial use subject to its license conditions,
          but does not require shared adaptations to remain under reciprocal
          licensing terms.
        </p>
        <p>
          Macro Evidence reviewed whether this repository should remain
          maximally permissive or operate as a reciprocal open-content commons.
          The review considered the repository's purpose, downstream-user
          clarity, current contribution history, third-party provenance,
          commercial reuse, licensing simplicity, and Macro Evidence's broader
          separation between rights in open work and rights in organizational
          identity.
        </p>
        <p>
          The repository is primarily community and participation infrastructure
          rather than product software. Its substantive materials define how
          people encounter, contribute to, report problems to, and participate
          in Macro Evidence. Small declarative GitHub configuration files also
          exist in the repository, but no material software codebase has been
          identified that would independently justify a software-specific
          repository license.
        </p>
        <p>
          Repository history reviewed for this decision did not identify
          external substantive contributions requiring separate relicensing
          permission. The current Code of Conduct incorporates third-party
          Contributor Covenant material and is handled separately rather than
          being silently relicensed by this decision.
        </p>
        <p>
          Existing CC BY 4.0 grants remain valid under their terms. This
          decision does not revoke or retroactively replace those grants.
        </p>
        <h2 id="decision">Decision</h2>
        <p>
          Beginning with implementation of this decision, publish the
          maintained&#32;<code>macro-evidence/.github</code>&#32;repository and
          future revisions under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
          International (CC BY-SA 4.0).
        </p>
        <p>
          Macro Evidence treats its organization-wide community and
          participation infrastructure as a reciprocal open-content commons. The
          material remains available for use, redistribution, adaptation, and
          commercial reuse, while adaptations that are shared must comply with
          the ShareAlike requirements of CC BY-SA 4.0 or an applicable
          compatible license.
        </p>
        <p>
          The repository's committed&#32;<code>LICENSE</code>&#32;remains the
          canonical license text for the current repository state.
        </p>
        <p>
          Macro Evidence's trademarks, names, marks, visual identity, official
          identifiers, and official status remain governed separately by the
          Trademarks Policy. Rights granted by the repository license do not
          themselves grant permission to present a fork, adaptation, service, or
          other use as official Macro Evidence.
        </p>
        <p>
          This decision applies only to&#32;<code>macro-evidence/.github</code>.
          It does not change the licenses of&#32;<code
            >macro-evidence/governance</code
          >,&#32;<code>macro-evidence/website</code>,&#32;<code
            >macro-evidence/macro-data-observatory</code
          >, data obtained or produced through Macro Data Observatory, or Macro
          Evidence's trademark and identity rights.
        </p>
        <h2 id="consequences">Consequences</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            The&#32;<code>.github</code>&#32;repository moves from CC BY 4.0 to
            CC BY-SA 4.0 for its maintained current and future releases.
          </li>
          <li>
            Commercial use, redistribution, and adaptation remain permitted
            under CC BY-SA 4.0.
          </li>
          <li>Shared adaptations are subject to ShareAlike requirements.</li>
          <li>
            Downstream users receive one repository-wide content-licensing model
            rather than needing different default licenses for individual
            community-health materials.
          </li>
          <li>
            Historical material already made available under CC BY 4.0 remains
            usable under those previously granted terms.
          </li>
          <li>
            Third-party material is not relicensed merely by changing the
            repository default; its applicable upstream terms must continue to
            be respected.
          </li>
          <li>
            The organization-wide Code of Conduct remains a separate policy
            decision and may be revised or replaced independently of this
            licensing decision.
          </li>
          <li>
            The website, MDO, governance, data, and trademark licensing
            questions remain governed by their own existing decisions and
            policies.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <div class="reference-links">
        <a class="text-link" href="/governance/decisions">
          All Governance decisions →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
